<title>USA: Tucson Electric Power Co Q1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Tucson Electric Power Co Q1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>TUCSON, Ariz. 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter Ended March 31			     1997	 1996</p>
<p> Utility operating revenues		    $154,281  $148,028</p>
<p> Net income					    11,492	 419</p>
<p> Average common shares outstanding (000)     32,135    32,134</p>
<p> Net income per average share of common stock  0.36	0.01</p>
<p> 12 Months Ended March 31			   1997	 1996</p>
<p> Utility operating revenues		    $722,126  $675,852</p>
<p> Net income					   131,925    70,284</p>
<p> Average common shares outstanding (000)     32,134    32,135</p>
<p> Net income per average share of common stock  4.11	2.19</p>
<p>NOTE: 1997 Q1 includes a gain of $14.3 million net benefit from net operating loss carryforward.</p>
<p>1996 12 month results include a $12.2 million pre-tax gain related to fuel contracts.</p>
<p>1997 twelve month results include a $10.6 million net pre-tax expense related to the Voluntary Severance Program and a $9.2 million pre-tax sales tax expense from an unfavorable court ruling.</p>
<p>Pre-tax gains relating to investment subsidiaries were $9.5 million for 1997 twelve month results and $0.6 million for 1996 twelve month results.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
</text>
